This repository publishes data, not software.

Its content is dated, immutable datasets under datasets/<date>/, and an errata
file per dataset under errata/. The only executable code is
scripts/validate-dataset.mjs and scripts/check-immutable.mjs, with their tests
scripts/check-validator.mjs and scripts/check-errata.mjs, all run by
.github/workflows/validate.yml on every pull request, which is the check that
actually matters here: a dataset is verified by its validator and its
immutability guard, not by a CLI walkthrough.

Scope, stated because a repo-root file cannot express it: this opt-out is for
DATA commits. A change to scripts/ or to the workflow is a change to the thing
that certifies every dataset in here, and should get the full review despite
this file.
